---
source: tests/cli_matrix.rs
expression: render(stringify! (global))
---
$ mdd -f human -h
exit: 0
--- stdout
Markdown-Driven Development -- structural queries for coding agents

Usage: mdd [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  toc    Table of contents with offset/limit annotations. Works on single files and directories
  sec    Extract section content by heading match. When path is a directory, searches across all .md files
  at     Find the section containing a given line number. Prints breadcrumb path to stderr
  map    Compressed structural overview for agent orientation. Shows hot files, directory structure, frontmatter stats, link graph
  find   Cross-file structural query with composable filters
  fm     Frontmatter inspection (read-only)
  links  Link graph extraction and validation
  agg    Aggregate matching sections into a single context-efficient output
  parts  List/filter entries in multi-frontmatter documents
  stats  Directory statistics: file counts, frontmatter coverage, types
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -f, --format <FORMAT>  Output format: human (colored), agent (provenance+signature), json [possible values: human, agent, json]
      --strict           Fail on first malformed file instead of skipping with a warning
      --all-files        Include AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, CLAUDE.local.md and README.md in directory scans
  -h, --help             Print help (see more with '--help')
  -V, --version          Print version
--- stderr

